Data Binding: 

1. String interpolation. {{}}
2. property binding. []
3. 2 way binding using ngModel. [()]
4. Event binding. ()

=> String interpolation is the process of binding the date in the html file from ts.
Ex: <p>{{name}}</p>

=> If we want to bind the value in the input field we have property binding to bind the value.
Ex: <input type = "text" [value]="name" />
=> In this we able to set the type of the field also like attributes
Ex: <input [type] = "inputType" />

-- Here string interpolation and property binding is the one way data binding 

=> For 2 way data binding we have ngModel that is present in the FormModule.
=> To use it we need to import in the ts file, imports.
Ex: <input type = "text" [(ngModel)]="name" />

=> Two way data binding is generally used in input elements.

=> for event binding we need to bind like this 
Ex: <button (ngModel)="save()">save</button>

Directives:

1. Structural (ngIf, ngFor)
3. Behavioural (ngClass, ngStyle)

=> Structural directives are used to change the structure of the dom.
=> Like based on some inputs the dom structure will going to change.
EX: <div *ngIf="condition">Test2</div> // here we can pass true or false inside the ngIf or else we can also check the condition inside the ngIf.
    <ul>
	<li *ngFor="let item in roles">{{item.roleName}</li>  //Here which element we want to repeat that element we have to use ngFor
    </ul>

=> In modern we have @if, @for for nfIf and ngFor directives we can use it.
=> here we no need to import any thing to use not like normal directives.

Api calling:
